    "label": "Saudi Arabia / GCC Strategic Positioning",
    "description": "The Gulf Cooperation Council's collective posture, led by Saudi Arabia. The GCC states face contradictory pressures: they share US concern over Iranian hegemony, host critical US bases (Al Udeid in Qatar, Ali Al Salem in Kuwait, NSA Bahrain, Al Dhafra in UAE), and benefit from Iranian military degradation. Yet normalization with Iran (Saudi-Iran Beijing Agreement, March 2023) creates incentives for restraint, and Arab publics are hostile to open alignment with Israel. Saudi Arabia's Vision 2030 requires stable oil revenues and foreign investment — a prolonged war is economically damaging regardless of the price spike. The GCC must also calculate whether to allow basing access to the US (which Iran would target) or formally deny it to maintain plausible neutrality.",
