    "description": "Turkey's response as a NATO member with unique equidistance between Washington and Tehran. Turkey maintains significant trade and energy ties with Iran (Iran is a major gas supplier), hosts NATO's Incirlik Air Base and Kürecik radar site, and has pursued an autonomous foreign policy under Erdogan that has included mediating between Russia and Ukraine. Turkey could be a critical swing actor: denying NATO basing access (or conditioning it) would significantly complicate US logistics; facilitating mediation could shorten the conflict; overt neutrality would signal a fracture in NATO cohesion that Russia and China would exploit. Turkey's NATO Article 5 obligations do not apply since no NATO member has been attacked.",
